Hello, I am hoping for help with post-stratification:
I have line transect data for butterflies. I would like to use a global detection function to estimate density in strata that represent sampling periods of the data because
1. I have very few detections in some strata (<10)
2. The butterflies are short-lived. My strata consist of 6-day sample periods, which I wish to estimate separate densities for. (I imagine this is very similar to post-stratifying a multi-year data set to create annual population estimates of a longer-lived animal)
I have been able to post-stratify my data using the column Observation>Label, which consists of the labels 1-14, as I have 14 sampling periods (Screenshots attached).

When I run the analysis, I get very low estimates of density. I believe it is because my line lengths are indicative of total sampling effort (in metres) on each transect throughout the entire season, rather than during each sampling period.

How can I restructure my data to 1. still provide a global detection function and 2. accurately reflect the line length surveyed in each strata (sampling period)?

