Dear Eric,
we have time and spatial series  of Perpendicular distance data from orangutan survey. and we want to show the result of the density/population automatically updated in our miniserver website which we only input the perpendicular data only, so we need to write the formula in our script. would you like to share insight how to write ESW formula in our script?

thank you

On Thu, Nov 30, 2023 at 3:43 PM Eric Rexstad <Eric.R...@st-andrews.ac.uk> wrote:
> Ahmad
>
> It is not simple to calculate detection probability (p) by hand; that is why we developed the Distance for Windows software. As I noted, the estimate of (p) is shown in the output you provided.
>
> To calculate (p) by hand, you would need to integrate the detection function with the estimated detection function shape (and perhaps scale) parameters.
>
>
>
